    [module name=http     gate=enforced reason='L7 HTTP/1.1 client+server on net (ENFORCED, all 64 cases green): PURE introspection (status/ok/header/headers/headers-named/has-body/body-bytes/body-bytes-wire/body-text) over homoiconic [request]/[response] literals — header value renders quoted when numeric-looking (value=\'1\') else bareword (value=c), `headers` is a node-sequence, absent header is () the absence channel, present-empty header /@value is \'\' vs absent (), body-bytes is a quoted string scalar; every network verb (get/post/put/del/patch/head/options/request/send, serve/listen/accept-iter/exchange-request/respond/stop) gated on `net` via cap_guard (CXER0271 deny-lane) with the granted lane asserting the deterministic synthetic shapes ([response status=200]/[http-server]/[request]/null); pure arg/scheme validation surfaces CXER4525 (non-http(s)/relative url=, bad bind URL), CXER4539 (status-on-request, url/path misuse, CONNECT, bad method), CXER4541 (respond status ∉ 100-599), CXER4532 (body-text unsupported charset) ahead of the cap check. ONE spec contradiction logged: §3.1 bad base-url at `client` → CXER4525 is not surfaced (impl reads opts off attrs, not the {} map), so it is fixtured at `send` instead (SPEC-FINDINGS). Live round-trips (real status/headers/body, TLS, redirects, gzip/zstd decompression) are gate=pending for a network-granted harness. §3.6 SSE/streaming landed (http-065..078): server sse/send-event/heartbeat/stream-open + client sse-connect/sse-events/source-open/last-event-id share one pure [event] framing codec (symmetry invariant in vcx/tests/http_sse_test.v); pure accessors + event validation (CXER4539 empty / CXER4531 CR-LF) + net-denial (CXER0271) + synthetic wire decode round-trip enforced; live held-open transport pending. §3.7 THE WEBSOCKET UPGRADE (#1086, RULED: INT-17, INT-19) is SPEC-FIRST and its seven cases (http-090..096) each carry their OWN gate=advisory: there is no ws-handshake, ws-confirm, ws-connect or ws-accept on this tree and no cx-stdlib/ws beneath them, so they are RED by construction and that red list IS the worklist. They grade the PURE half — the whole decision a handshake makes is a function of two messages, so ws-handshake answers the 101 and its accept from a server-received [request] and ws-confirm reads the key a client sent against the [response] it got — plus the net-denial lane for ws-connect. The FRAMES are not graded here at all: they are cx-stdlib/ws\'s and live in conformance/stdlib/ws.cxd. Ten codes are allocated out of the CXER4552-4589 block §8 reserved for exactly this before the section existed, CXER4552..CXER4561; 4562-4589 stays reserved. Flip to enforced in the commit that lands §3.7']
