    [module name=ws       gate=advisory reason='SPEC-FIRST FRONTIER — the Ring 1 PURE WebSocket FRAME CODEC (spec/03-approved/stdlib/ws.md, status=new; #1086, RULED: INT-17, INT-19) is specced and UNIMPLEMENTED: there is no stdlib/ws.cx and no vcx/code/stdlib_ws.v, so all 54 cases are RED by construction and that red list IS the implementation worklist (the audit #1422, connector #1430, sync #1434, graphql #1429 and soap #1456 precedent, RULED: S-2). The corpus is hermetic and every one of the eleven public defs is Ring 1 and PURE — one RFC 6455 frame encoded and decoded with the octet count it consumed, a buffer read into the frames it carries and the remainder it does not, the masking transform applied, a message fragmented at a bound and assembled back, the three control frames built and read, a close frame read into its code and reason, a text message answered as a string only when it is valid UTF-8, and the handshake\'s Sec-WebSocket-Accept derived — so no case carries a grant=, a port, a store URL or --manual-clock, and none reaches cx-platform/net or cx-platform/http: the upgrade EXCHANGE is http.md §3.7\'s and the walk over the events is the connector kit\'s kind=stream adapter (connector.md §3.15). NOT A SECOND DIGEST AND NOT A SECOND ENCODER: the SHA-1 is crypto.md §3.8\'s and the base64 is bytes\', and this module assembles the accept derivation over them and implements neither. THE ATTACK FAMILY IS FIRST IN THE FILE because it was written first: ws-001 … 015 are the fifteen classes of the spec §5.1 — a payload over the bound, an unmasked client frame, a masked server frame, a reserved bit with no negotiated extension, an unassigned opcode, invalid UTF-8 in a text frame, a fragmented control frame, a control payload over 125 octets, a one-octet close body, a close code outside the admitted set, a continuation with no start, a data frame inside a fragmented message, an assembled message over the bound, a non-minimal length form, and a buffer shorter than the frame declares. Then ws-020 … 029 the frame and its three length forms, ws-030 … 034 the masking transform, ws-040 … 046 fragmentation and assembly, ws-050 … 056 the control frames and the close codes, ws-060 … 063 the UTF-8 rule that belongs to the MESSAGE and not to the frame, ws-070 … 072 the accept derivation, and ws-080 … 082 the bounds at their edges. Every expectation is derived from one in-tree fixture the corpus states once and every octet string in it is RFC 6455 §5.7\'s or §1.3\'s own worked example, so a reader checks the file against the standard rather than against its author. Twelve codes are allocated with this corpus, CXER6900..CXER6911 inside the band governance.md §9.6 registers for this module — NOT the next free block: 6700–6899 is sftp\'s and ftp\'s on the unmerged #1457/#1458 branch and is stepped over rather than reused. Flip to enforced in the commit that lands the code']
