    [module name=bus gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 37 cases green): in-process pub/sub with synchronous, deterministic, ordered dispatch (descending priority, ties by registration order, §4.1) + re-entrant FIFO emission queue drained before the next external message (§4.2) + bounded cascade (max-cascade-depth/events → CXER4663, §4.4) + on-fault :isolate/:collect/:halt (§4.3); bus/close/on/off + introspection subscribers/topics/match/topic/matches; emit returns a [dispatch …] VALUE (zero subscribers → delivered=0, not a fault/absence, §2.3); [bus]/[subscription] closeable via [?with-open]. bus introduces NO capability (§5). The §2.2 prefix-glob runs in the spec-native spelling (:order.* matches :order.placed) since the #397 dotted-atom ruling retired the earlier dash-separator workaround; the CXPath-predicate pattern form is realized as a pure arity-1 boolean callable. CXER4661 (handle-race) is unreachable single-threaded.']
    [module name=fabric gate=enforced reason='P0 embedded tier complete + spec-faithful (spec/02-working/fabric.md, #518/#531): durable plane composed over journal (publish→append receipt, subscribe/receive batched pull filtered by the bus §2.2 pattern vocabulary reused verbatim, ack = cumulative committed offset persisted as store data via the journal-store doc-backed-alias pattern — at-least-once proven by the uncommitted-tail-redelivers + offset-is-store-data lanes) + transient plane (latest-wins channels); observe = read-only (ack → CXER4922); no capability of its own (mem:// hermetic); journal attribution/lifecycle errors surface verbatim (composition honesty lane). Band CXER4920-4949; served tier P1 / coord migration P2 / adapters P3 pending.']
    [module name=live gate=enforced reason='W1 stateless core shipped + spec-faithful (stream 3, #675; pack spec spec/02-working/live.md): [$live:changes-since] over the L99 quoted-planar pipeline widened to store AND journal sources under an explicit $bind formal-name map; head-set cursor (profile §5.1 spelling; store pos = the #708 store:log docs-plane advance seq, journal pos = the stream seq); exact ∂ inside the L101 incremental sub-fragment via planar_delta feed (insert/retract/regroup, apply-order coordinates, ROW ≡ recompute row — L131 transparency), the honest [recompute reason=…]+full-relation form outside it, and full-relation-as-inserts from the EMPTY cursor for every comprehension (equivalence-quartet leg 1). Both paths behind the eval capability (L99 posture, effect_alignment row). Refusals: CXER5070 not-planar / CXER0120 membership reused / CXER5071 unbound-or-mis-kinded formal / CXER5072 invalid cursor (incl. two-streams-one-formal) / CXER5073 below-retention (post-prune history loss; blob history fail-closes the same way) / CXER4700 authz reused / CXER1709 reused for non-objgraph + named-wire-ref stores (the W5 store-feed wave completes per-ref). observe/materialize/advance/read land W2/W3.']
    [module name=supervise gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 30 cases green at landing (24 behavior/negative + 6 fn-doc-backing); RULED: SUP-1, #765): pure-CX supervision loop over [?worker]/[?monitor]/fan-out channels/sched — restart types (:permanent/:transient/:temporary) × outcomes, exp backoff + intensity window + attempt-reset on the mock clock (fixtures barrier timer-arming via a status round-trip — ops queue behind terminal notes in the one inbox), :one-for-all/:rest-for-one cancel-reverse/restart-in-order byte-pinned, intensity counts DECISIONS not respawns, give-up cancels-all + [gave-up] final + CXER5094 in the loop panic cause chain (parents escalate by composition — the tree case), stop reverse + idempotent, [?with-open] auto-stop joins the loop to [stopped], dynamic start-child/stop-child, status snapshots (readable post-stop via the keep=1 cell), CXER5090/5091/5093 negatives. The wedged-child abandon arm rides vcx/tests/stdlib_supervise_test.v (SUP-1f: [?cancel] stamps the terminal at request, .cxd cannot observe shutdown expiry); the events-laggard CXER0218 arm is the core channel STREAM_GAP contract (SUP-1b).']
    [module name=journal gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful: append-only hash-chained tenant-partitioned event log + deterministic fold→state, built ON store (persistence) + hash (chain links) + crypto.ed25519 (snapshot signing); no new capability (gated by store). open/attach/close, append (single mutating verb, optimistic expect-pos → CXER1114), read/slice/since/query/head (out-of-range = absence (), not null/err), fold/fold-slice/fold-value/replay/dry-run (pure $fn enforced via the journal_stdlib_builtin_env eval-hook + node_calls_impure_builtin → CXER4611), verify/verify-slice (a present [verification valid=…] FINDING, not [err] — SAP §1; hash-mismatch/link-broken/seq-gap/genesis-invalid reasons), snapshot (signed [snapshot] over fold+anchor)/snapshot-verify/fold-from (fold ≡ full fold)/retain (prune-behind-signed-snapshot → CXER4616)/compact (copy-forward, source intact). Hermetic mem:// fixtures with a controllable clock so ts/hash are byte-stable']
    [module name=session gate=enforced reason='full §3 (principal,tenant) session impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green): the thin XAP session layer COMPOSES the shipped cx-stdlib/crypto jwt-verify (token verification delegated ENTIRELY, §2.2/N-SESSION-1) + cx-platform/http (Authorization/Cookie header reads + Set-Cookie writes) — session adds NO crypto and NO transport. FAIL-CLOSED attach (verify→map→bind→mirror-attach all-or-nothing); the four-channel split honored (unattached of→absence () NOT null NOT err; rejected attach→[err]; established→[session] value). Server-held registry (mirror-attach, by-id/by-client/of/from-cookie); opaque session id + CSRF synchronizer token are CSPRNG (never asserted by literal value — fixtures pin prefix/length/round-trip). CAPABILITY-FREE (no new cap, no effect_alignment entry — only net reach is crypto JWKS fetch). Error band CXER4800-4849: 4801 token-reject (wraps verbatim crypto fault as [cause]), 4802 no-tenant, 4803 no-principal, 4804 invalid/detached-op, 4805 rebind-refused (immutable binding), 4806 insecure-transport, 4807 no-token, 4808/4809 csrf-missing/mismatch, 4810/4811 cookie-insecure/unsafe-flags. Hermetic: reuses the crypto-071 golden RS256 token + literal JWKS + pinned now=[$time:datetime 2023 11 14 22 13 20]; tenant derived from the aud claim (no tid in the golden token).']
    [module name=sso gate=enforced reason='the enterprise-SSO DEPLOYMENT surface (#1394, epic S item S7, RULED: 1394-a) — ENFORCED from the first case, because every one of them is a REFUSAL a route surface exists to make and a refusal nobody grades is a hole. PURE CX over oidc/saml/scim/session/store/url/json/crypto: no native primitive, no capability of its own, no second parser (a form body IS a query string, so url:query-parse reads it — rider 3). The corpus runs OFFLINE because every verb is a function from a [request …] literal to a [response …] and everything that must survive the redirect is in the mem:// store seam: the whole park/take/refuse cycle, the open redirect in three spellings (absolute, protocol-relative //evil, and a CR-LF response split), the RelayState redirect, a SAMLResponse that is not base64 (bytes CXER2302, propagated unchanged), a body past the ceiling refused BEFORE the decode, a smuggled duplicate form field pinned to one value, four bearer refusals including a PREFIX of the configured token and the fail-closed unset-token default, an unbound logout, and a real signed assertion establishing a real cookie session end to end. Refusals are ANSWERED as responses carrying their code — a mounted handler that RAISED would produce a 500 and an opaque body — so the cases read $r/body/err@code; the three out-err cases are exactly the three that are not request-shaped (CXER6006 the deployment own defect, and the [auth] guard, which returns the [err] VALUE because that is what [auth EXPR] consumes). The two legs that genuinely dial — oidc:complete token POST and RFC 7009 revocation — are graded by make test-sso-interop-lane in two processes against examples/platform/sso/deployment/, never here (oidc.md §6, and the #973 blocking-accept hazard).']
    [module name=authz gate=enforced reason='full §3 decision-layer impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green): the single PEP decision function check/authorize over principals + attenuating/time-bounded/revocable delegations + guardian grants behind an incapacity-typed [gate …], plus the signed+versioned 6-predicate incapacity library, verify-tier (T0/T1/T2 M-of-N), effective envelope (intersection, most-restrictive-wins, unrecorded relationship ignored), dry-run/explain/trace. COMPOSES crypto/session/journal/store — adds NO crypto, NO transport, NO new caps-capability (capability-free in-memory store, no effect_alignment entry, mirroring session/journal). FOUR-CHANNEL: a decision is a present [permit]/[deny] VALUE (deny carries CXER4700 as DATA, NOT an [err]); check is TOTAL; an absent (revoked/expired/never-issued) grant is the absence channel () NOT null NOT [deny]; null is never produced. FAIL-CLOSED deny-by-default; guardian permits ONLY while its incapacity gate holds + ONLY its pinned [action …], flipping to [deny] the instant the principal re-engages (falsifiable-by-presence, no explicit revoke). BRIGHT LINE as a type constraint at AUTHORING: refusal-trigger leaf → CXER4701, state-only gate (<1 incapacity) → CXER4702, inline/ad-hoc predicate → CXER4706, escalation → CXER4703, T0-guardian/bad-sig/quorum-unmet → CXER4704, guardian↔ordinary shape mismatch + cross-tenant delegate + missing tenant → CXER4711, closed store → CXER4712. ONE grammar adaptation: the spec verb gate-wellformed? is spelled gate-wellformed (no trailing ?) — ? is not a NameChar in a call head [$authz:VERB …], the same constraint that forced net addr->string→addr-to-string (semantics identical, returns a [valid]/[invalid] VALUE not an [err]). Hermetic in-memory store + deterministic clock via as-of/until Unix-int + recorded signature markers (non-empty/non-invalid verifies T1; M-of-N quorum for T2) so negatives are testable without minting keys.']
    [module name=sched gate=enforced reason='full §3 durable-scheduler impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 44 cases green): after/at/every(fixed-delay|fixed-rate)/recur(a time [recurrence …] rule)/cron/cancel/timer-state + restore + test-clock-advance/clock-mode. sched is a THIN module that COMPOSES three shipped modules and adds NO calendar grammar, NO persistence, and NO new capability (§0/§5): time (next-occurrence re-arm + parse-cron + ::duration/::datetime), journal (durable [sched-intent …] append + restore fold), the picoev loop. Firing is $ev-shape-dispatched (§2.1): a callable is invoked on the loop (return ignored) — with no arguments when it is zero-arg, and with the FIRE INSTANT when it declares one parameter (sched-044, #1358 question 5, RULED: 1358-e), read from the clock that armed the timer, which is the deadline of the timer itself under the manual drain; a [?channel] gets a [tick timer=<name>] posted, and the tick carries NO instant — giving it one changes twenty prior expectations, drafted as 1358-f and not landed. The DETERMINISTIC surface is enforced under the :manual virtual clock (virtual-now starts at the epoch; test-clock-advance drains due timers in deadline order, sleep-free, §4.2); the :wall PRODUCTION clock is no longer deferred (#1358, RULED: 1358-a..d) — it fires at the §2.6 SAFEPOINTS (the §10.5.4 blocking cancellation points and the blocking serve loops), owned by the arming lineage, and it is graded in the wall-clock lane vcx/timing/sched_wall_clock_test.v, NOT here: this corpus IS the :manual clock, so CXER4970 test-clock-under-:wall is unreachable from inside it by construction and its negative lives in that lane. The LIVE picoev held-open firing loop remains the synthetic-transport part and stays gate=pending for a runtime-driven harness. on-missed (§2.5/§4.6): a single advance crossing N occurrences fires once under :skip/:coalesce, once-per-occurrence under :fire-all (recur COUNT-3 observed via :fire-all). [timer] is closeable via [?with-open] (close ≡ cancel, idempotent, never CXER0108) — the arming verbs are env-aware to stamp the close-id. Durable worker-recycle correctness: a named timer appends its intent to a journal; restore folds the journal to re-arm pending timers, binding $ev by name from the registry, surfacing an unbound name as an orphaned FINDING in the [restore-report …] (never silently dropped, §3.2). on-missed DEFAULTS BY KIND (RULED: 1324-SK-2): :skip for a recurrence, :fire-all for a durable one-shot (after/at) — a recurrence has a next occurrence to skip to and a one-shot does not, and the effective policy is stamped into the persisted intent at the arm so a journal is self-describing (sched-022) with a per-kind fallback for intents written before it (sched-042). Under an explicit :skip a past one-shot is NOT re-armed and is NOT silent: named in a [dropped [drop name= kind= deadline=]] block AND closed in the journal with status \'dropped\', so it is dropped once rather than re-reported at every boot (sched-040 restores twice to pin the close); the drop decision runs AFTER the registry lookup, so a FOREIGN pending intent this process does not bind stays orphaned and untouched rather than being buried (sched-043); and :fire-all re-arms it at its PERSISTED deadline, never the boot instant, so it fires once, late, on the next turn of the clock (sched-041). Error band CXER4970-4989: 4971 arg-invalid, 4972 mode/on-missed-invalid, 4973 durable-no-name, 4974 durable-no-journal, 4975 restore-intent-corrupt; a malformed cron surfaces time\'s CXER33xx unchanged (not a sched code); a raw effect in a fired callback without a grant hits CXER0271 at the callback effect point. Hermetic: :manual clock + mem:// journal so ts/hash/fires are byte-stable.']
    [module name=flow gate=enforced reason='WAVE 1 of the general workflow module (#1265; RULED: WF-0..WF-17 + #1260 CA-1..CA-4 + 1265-PB/PC/PD) — ENFORCED, every case green; W1 SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (packets A-D). PURE CX over journal/authz/sched/cx apart from ONE module-internal Ring-2 act seam ([$flow-perform], RULED: 1265-PB-1), no engine process and no capability of its own. What is enforced here: `validate` over §2.3\'s CLOSED vocabulary — eighteen words since vocabulary round 2 (RULED: WF-18 … WF-26) and RULED: WF-42, of which TEN are implemented — the W1 nine plus `needs=` (RULED: 789-WF-20a) — the §7 applicability matrix cell by cell, the refusals register row by row (make-style FILE dependency words WF-16, retry POLICY, do=/[fn]/[args {…}] as third spellings of the act CA-2, per-step compensators, triggers WF-3, decision tables, approver LISTS and delegation, UNBOUNDED loops, sub-flow as NESTING, unknown words/attributes), and — flow-009, the #1323 drift guard — the SEVEN round-2 words this wave does not run (`until`, `quorum=`, `flow=`, `[notify]`, `calendar=`, `attempts=`, `every=`) refused NAMING their landing rather than reciting a reason §2.3 has withdrawn, the same shape the W3 performer axis uses, duration literals decided by the reader\'s TYPE rather than a hand parser, name uniqueness, branch/[seq]/map nesting (branch-in-branch flattened), the §4.7 pivot rules (one per TREE, none inside a branch, pre-pivot [compensates] pairing read off the resolver, no-pivot ⇒ fully compensable), the §4.4 guard DOMAIN + CXPath-ness (an infix comparison refuses naming the prefix form), §4.1 act resolution (CXER4953), and the resolver/args caller faults (CXER4965); `simulate` — the §4.2 runner law from a fresh record over a supplied [results …] table: completion, parking on a missing result (no second effect — the same rule that makes N advancers ONE effect), guards recorded as :skipped, branch JOIN-ALL and lane failure, map :fanned-out with the parent stream O(1) per map, pre-pivot compensation in reverse COMPLETION order and post-pivot forward-only incomplete=N; `fold-record` — the pinned fold identity from [flow-transition …] entries to the [flow-run …] record with locator triples, the absence channel on an empty sequence. AND, from vocabulary round 2 (RULED: 789-WF-20a): `needs=` — ORDER over PRECEDING SIBLINGS, which RELAXES document order into a DAG and never creates one, so siblings whose needs are met activate together while a construct with no `needs=` keeps §4.3\'s default wait on its immediate predecessor; a FORWARD, self, cross-boundary, unknown or empty name refuses CXER4952 saying WHICH (a cycle is unrepresentable, so there is no cycle detector), and the JUSTIFICATION is a measured gate row rather than an opinion — flow-017 carries BOTH the `needs=` build DAG and the equivalent nested join-all `branch` document and simulates each with one compile parked: the DAG drives five of seven steps, the level-structured document three, and both complete when every result is supplied. THE PERFORMER AXIS IS W3: by= other than :runner, to=, [escalate] and [bounds] refuse CXER4952 with a message naming the wave (the ruled staging — a value, never silence), so §2.1\'s document is fixtured in its W1 runner-only form. AND, from packets B-D: start/advance/status over the journal — the run id as the content address over (document, actor, nonce) with the args OUTSIDE the preimage (PB-2), the home stream = the run id verbatim (PB-3), one advance = ONE effect and its outcome under ONE CAS append (PB-6), the §4.8 compensation triple over REAL acts through the def\'s [compensates] pairing, `deadline=` as a durable sched timer, the [requires-at] admission bracket at the act seam, the record AS the durable step-dedup ([deduped …] for every terminal state), the racing-courier CAS path, and `map` fanning out into child runs in their own streams under a recorded cursor and max-parallel= (PC-1: the parent\'s cost per CHILD is O(1)). AND, from #1322 (RULED: 789-WF-27a): LIVENESS — `deadline=` arms with `on-missed :fire-all` pinned by timer kind rather than relying on sched\'s own default (belt-and-braces since RULED: 1324-SK-2 made :fire-all the default for a durable ONE-SHOT that names no policy; flow states its own liveness guarantee rather than depending on another module\'s default), and the public `rearm` verb is the restore half a live runner calls at boot: it folds the journal to the pending [sched-intent …] set, DERIVES each registry entry from the timer\'s own name (`<run id>:<step>`, the fire value always `advance` with [timer-fired run= step= at=] — 1265-PB-5) and calls sched restore, so a deadline pending across a RESTART is re-armed and fires, a deadline that ELAPSED while the process was down fires exactly once at boot carrying its ORIGINAL persisted instant rather than the boot instant, an empty journal answers [restore-report rearmed=0] as a VALUE, a durable intent flow did not arm stays ORPHANED rather than being re-armed by a runner that does not own it, and — the negative that pins the defect — the same restart WITHOUT `rearm` leaves every intent orphaned in the [restore-report …] and fires nothing. Those cases start from the state a CRASHED advancer leaves (a run parked `:running` plus its pending intent, and NO live timer in this process), which is the class flow-036 cannot reach because there the closure is still live. fleet/migrate/claim/release/reassign/resolve land in later waves and the snapshot-anchored reader is wave item W1-E — a missing verb is not a stub (§1.1 names the wave each lands in). Hermetic: every case runs over mem:// with a synthetic clock — no file I/O, no network, no capability grant; `flow=` is the document\'s Tier-1 content address, byte-stable across hosts. SEVEN cases carry their OWN gate=advisory and are the one spec-first family here: flow-080..086, the RECORD BINDING RULE (flow.md §4.4) and the TRANSFORM step `[compute …]` (§4.4a), RULED: WF-42 — the spec landed ahead of the runner code on purpose (the connector #1430 and sync #1434 precedent), so those seven are RED by construction and that list IS the implementation worklist; they flip to enforced in the commit that lands the binding at activation and the execution of the transform step. The two claims a single-process fixture cannot hold — real `cx` PROCESSES relaying one run, and the `cx flow` command line\'s argv/exit codes/stdout-stderr split (RULED: 1265-PD-1) — are vcx/tests/flow_umbrella_test.v.']
    [# XAP grammar composition — M0 composition engine. #]
    [module name=xap-compose gate=enforced reason='M0 composition engine landed (ENFORCED, all 26 cases green): [$xap:compose]/[$xap:compose-report]/[$xap:resolve]/[$xap:grammar-hash] as PURE env-free builtins (vcx/code/stdlib_xap.v — no journal, no PEP, no clock) per xap_grammar_composition.md §8.1. compose: N-COMPOSE-0 qualification by construction, W1-W6 gate reporting EVERY violation as [conflict code=:wN at= detail=] (W1 name-uniqueness; W2 key type agreement resolved through the registering nouns\' field types; W3 frame via→field existence + family coordinate type geo=geo-point/time=instant|interval/value=ordered-scalar; W4 mandate↔exclusion (verb,when) contradiction + ordering-cycle detection per SCC + dependency-target existence + rule scope-reach own-feature/uses-set; W5 uses/constituent existence + §6 signature-weakening (declared below the derived floor rejected; absent adopts the floor) + constituent-cycle; W6 total by construction of the bare-term index); structurally identical duplicate features collapse (§3.1 idempotence) while same-name-different-content stays a W1 reject; output [grammar …] ⊢ grammar.cxs emitted fully sorted so the same feature SET yields byte-identical canonical form → same Tier-1 hash (commutativity/associativity fixtures hold by determinism). compose-report: never raises on conflicts, agreement law shared via the one gate fn. resolve: ρ with qualified-bypass, unique-owner, focus→arg-nouns→present narrowing (a non-decisive empty narrowing keeps the prior candidate set), CXER4871 ambiguity carries candidates= sorted, CXER4872 unknown carries term=. CXER4873 for any non-[feature] argument (structural feature.cxs-grade validation of everything the engine reads; full .cxs schema validation joins when the draft schemas graduate). Five spec-first authoring defects re-derived against the real engine (the single-oracle rule): 4 cases used an invented `[?[= …]]` path-predicate form — rewritten to the grammar [132] attribute-test `[@name=\'…\']`, whose projection renders the WRAPPED attribute node ([effect \'arrange\'] / [derived true] / [candidates \'…\'], matching the code.cxd cxpath-predicate convention) — and the resolve noun-narrowing case exposed that list literals travel as __cx_arr__ marker elements (engine flatten now descends them like __cx_seq__). Family 6 (N-COMPOSE-2 / §8.2 runtime integration, cases 027-036) LANDED with the M0 residue: [$xap:run {grammar: G}] pins the composed grammar as the runtime control vocabulary; every emit then resolves through ρ (the committed journal event is QUALIFIED; surviving ambiguity CXER4871 with candidates=, unknown CXER4872) and a derived verb is PEP-admitted by its TRANSITIVE LEAF constituent grant set (xap_gc_leaf_grants) — a wrapper-name grant conveys nothing, the CXER4850 denial names the missing constituent exactly as emitting it directly would; why-allowed answers over the same set (allowed=true iff every leaf decision permits, chains merged). Grammar-less runtimes keep the pre-composition cascade semantics (bundled-demo back-compat). All 36 cases green; the 10 family-6 in-code programs were parse-verified against the real binary at authoring time (the runner treats parse failure as PASS when out-err is set — the M0 phase-1 false-green vector).']
    [# XAP schema-as-data — the feature KIND whose nouns' fields are tenant-edited records (#1497). #]
    [module name=xap-schema gate=advisory reason='SPEC-FIRST FRONTIER - the schema-as-data FEATURE KIND (spec/03-approved/xap/xap_schema_as_data.md, status=new; #1497, RULED: SD-1) is specced and UNIMPLEMENTED: `kind=` on a [feature] carries `base` and `composite` on this tree, nothing synthesizes a schema noun or its four verbs, and there is no code for the kind in vcx/platform/stdlib_xap.v - so all 23 cases are RED by construction and that red list IS the implementation worklist (the audit #1422, connector #1430, sync #1434, graphql #1429 and soap #1456 precedent, RULED: S-2). WHAT THE KIND IS: a feature declaring kind=schema-as-data names ONE subject noun tenant-fields=true, and compose SYNTHESIZES onto it a schema noun whose RECORDS are that subject\'s tenant-edited fields, four verbs that write them (declare / widen / view / retire, each with a fixed name, effect signature and §6.1 parameter list), four named types and three rules. The tenant edits records; the tenant never edits the grammar - xap-schema-021 is the load-bearing case, the composed grammar\'s Tier-1 hash unmoved by a schema edit, which is connector.md §3.6\'s "discovery never changes the grammar" and CK-4\'s refusal of run-time grammar reads made mechanical. THE ATTACK CLASSES ARE FIRST IN THE FILE because they were written first: xap-schema-001...012 are a tenant field named to collide with a verb and with a compose-time field, a narrowing retype under live data, a schema over the field-count bound, a name over the octet bound, the two shapes of crossing a noun (:ref and a sibling noun\'s name), a schema edit that would add a verb and one that would change an effect, declare/retire churn against the bound, :geo-point as a tenant type, and a hidden field still offered as a facet. Then xap-schema-020...030 are the positive shapes: the synthesis read off the composed grammar, the stable hash, a data write validated against a tenant field and one refused by it, a field no schema record holds, an admitted widening, the [views] roles over a tenant field and the [group] clause with its dir (RULED: VG-3), the ux claim of a field compose never saw, the journal record of a schema edit, and a retired field omitted from a default projection with its data intact. NO CODE IS ADDED TO ANY BAND and that is stated rather than omitted: CXER4850-4879 is spent, 4880-4889 is xap-dist\'s and 4903-4919 is reserved for the served bridge\'s attribution surface (xap.md §8, governance.md §9.6), and every refusal this kind names is a class the ONE pre-commit enforcement point already raises with its meaning unchanged - CXER4869 the parameter list, CXER4867 a field type, CXER4868 a declared transition, CXER4865 a rule\'s [check]. Hermetic: every case composes the SAME board feature and runs an UNBOUND runtime (no port, no store URL, no grant=, no --manual-clock). Flip to enforced in the commit that lands the code.']
    [# XAP feature distribution — M1 P0 packages (spec/02-working/xap_feature_distribution_market.md §6.1). #]
    [module name=xap-dist gate=enforced reason='M1 P0 distribution engine landed (ENFORCED, all 24 cases green): pkg-tree (canonical sorted content doc — its store hash IS Tier-1) / pkg-seal (tag-object pattern: manifest beside the hashed tree) / pkg-sign (detached ed25519 over the Tier-1 hash by a publisher-DID key) / pkg-publish (alias name@version → manifest hash; released aliases immutable, CXER4887; unsigned publish refused, sign-from-day-one) / pkg-fetch (alias discovers, trust never rests on it; CXER4886) / pkg-verify (the §3 fail-closed chain: absent content 4886, divergent 4881 [honest-store-unreachable defense], unsigned/wrong-signer 4882, bad attestation VC 4883 w/ opts.now clock pin) / pkg-install (fetch→verify→PER-KIND gate→consent=grants→enable: features meet the ONE W1-W6 compose gate via xap_compose_builtin — conflicts carried through as [conflict] children of CXER4884; libraries meet the exports-surface check via the module loader OWN pass-1 scanner + computation identity recomputed via the pure relation (computes-as: claim, A4); consent issues EXACTLY the needs set as real AuthzDelegations, libraries get none (N-DIST-2); accepts a previous [installed] report for chaining) / pkg-requires-closure (code plane hash-pinned transitive closure, cycle 4880, missing 4886). Engine = vcx/code/stdlib_xap_dist.v composing store/did/vc/crypto/compose dispatchers ONLY — §9 absences enforced structurally by scripts/check_xap_dist_absences.py (make check-xap-dist-absences). Dogfood: case 016 seals/verifies/installs the REAL packages/gtin codec source; case 025 (M2) consumes the COMMITTED registry/ git-registry offline with pinned supply-chain-witness hashes; cases 026-028 (M3) = pkg-catalog discovery (alias-table authoritative locally; CXPath //publisher query pushdown on served stores — no alias verbs on the wire), term search over name+verb/noun/def surfaces, name@version resolution against the committed registry. The §4.2 stage-2 re-host invariance (catalog-discover + verify + install over a REAL loopback XSP-profile socket, hashes bit-identical to stage 1) is gated by the served-registry re-host section of vcx/tests/xap_umbrella_test.v (the #783 consolidation home). Cases 029-038 (M4) = entitlements: license = attenuating VC ([delegation [capabilities [enable]] [entitlement …]] rider via vc-issue — NO DRM subsystem, §9 absence 7): perpetual w/ version-range attenuation (M.x), subscription expires+grace-until (offline holders verify through term+grace; lapse = CXER4883 at the NEXT verify point, running XAPs untouched — N-DIST-1), per-seat org→principal delegation chain (parent VC embedded, seat>seats = attenuation violation, each seat offline-verifiable — the chain IS the count), bundle [members] coverage (non-member denied; install stays per-package), and install policy (opts.require-entitlement: absent VC denied; opts.entitlement verified as trust-chain stage 3.5) — price is a market property: the SAME committed gtin@0.1.0 artifact installs gratis (016/025) and under entitlement (038) with identical verification. Cases 039-044 (M5) = market+commerce: the market IS a XAP (market/*.feature.cxd compose through the ONE W-gate, 10 verbs, commerce/fulfil DERIVED over entitlement/issue-license); the order→settlement→fulfil choreography journals as qualified committed events (§8.2 emit resolution); 041 = the anti-laundering lane: the settlement gateway holding record-settlement AND EVEN the fulfil wrapper grant is CXER4850-denied naming the CONSTITUENT entitlement/issue-license (N-COMPOSE-2 doing commercial work); bundles = CATALOG OBJECTS ([bundle] docs listed by pkg-catalog, §5.3 — never composite features) with the bundle-REFERENCE entitlement resolved from the store at verify (042) and version-BOUND (043: growth = re-issuance, never silent expansion); federation = data (044: two market catalogs blend into one surface, installs verify at origin). Cases 061-067 (#1258, RULED: INT-13) are ENFORCED: the §5.3 bundle DOCUMENT - nesting via an includes block, the member-set CLOSURE, and the derivation rule that a tenant entitled member set is the closure of the bundles its VCs name - is specced with its schema spec/03-approved/xap/xap_schemas/bundle.cxs, and the code phase landed the closure function [$xap:bundle-members] (a depth-first walk over [includes] keyed on the resolved bundle name@version, duplicates collapsed on member identity and sorted by it, OPTS.require-catalog resolving every member package pin through pkg-catalog) plus the derivation rule inside license-verify, whose bundle-reference coverage check now reads the CLOSURE instead of the flat member list - which is why 042/043 moved onto the [members] block the schema declares. They were authored spec-first and advisory against a tree with no code, so the red list that was the worklist is the pass list (the xap-schema #1497 precedent, RULED: S-2). NO CODE IS ADDED TO ANY BAND: an include cycle is the cycle CXER4880 already names, an unresolvable include or an uncatalogued member pin the absent-from-the-store CXER4886, and an entitlement that does not cover the CXER4883 case 036 pins. cx xap init scaffolds the pair (a core pack and the suite that includes it) beside reference/shop's, so the shape is learned rather than invented. All in-code programs run standalone against the real binary at authoring (the parse-as-pass runner trap); 12 bracket-balance authoring defects caught exactly that way.']
    [# XAP serve — the [$xap:serve] option set (#1221 half b). #]
    [module name=xap-serve gate=enforced reason='RULED: 1221-b-1a, 1221-b-2a (ledger/rulings_2026_09_08_xap_serve_option_set_1221.md) - the [$xap:serve] CLOSED option set {runtime, tenant, shell, auth, block}, ENFORCED from the first case. Before #1221 half b, xap.md:236 promised that every [$xap:run] option is also accepted by serve, and nine of them (journal/authz/sessions/components/surfaces/handlers/resolver/sources/log-reduce) were read by NOBODY: a deployment writing {surfaces: (...)} on serve booted a server with no surfaces registered and no diagnostic, which is the silent acceptance the issue reports. The promise is deleted from the spec and the set is enforced in xap_serve as its FIRST act - before runtime resolution, before URL parsing, before cap_guard - so a misplaced key is refused by NAME with CXER4852 (the arg-shape code serve already owns) and the sentence: run options belong to [$xap:run]; pass the runtime via runtime:. Cases: 001 a genuine run key (surfaces) refused by name; 002 an unknown key (blocking) refused identically - a closed set, not a run-key blacklist; 003 all five keys accepted, proven by the call reaching the auth: validator, the first check after the guard; 004 the four non-auth keys accepted plus the portless-URL refusal that keeps this suite out of the socket engine. EVERY case uses a PORTLESS URL deliberately: the stdlib runner grants the FULL capability set to any case whose out-err does not name CXER0271, so a case reaching start_xap_listener would bind a real socket and, block defaulting to true, park the gate forever.']
    [# XAP intent handlers — [$xap:on] / [$xap:off] and the §4.1 handler cascade (#1294). #]
    [module name=xap-on gate=enforced reason='RULED: 1294-a…f, 1294-a2, 1294-g, 1294-h (ledger/rulings_2026_09_09_xap_on_intent_handlers_1294.md) - the verb\'s FIRST fixtures ever, ENFORCED from the first case. Before this landing [$xap:on] was a four-line stub that read none of its arguments and returned a null scalar, with a docstring claiming it "records the handler" and a XapRuntime carrying no handlers field: a scope=public verb that accepted a registration and discarded it, which is why every pattern shape in the report behaved identically. The corpus was SILENT (zero hits for xap:on anywhere in conformance/, docs-src/ or docs/llm/), so nothing was pinned and the design was open. What is enforced here: the four §4.5 pattern forms (verb atom, qualified verb string, [?quote]d act pattern whose $x holes BIND through the same engine [?match] uses, arity-1 predicate) with a bare verb matching a qualified act\'s local name and a qualified pattern exact; the [subscription id=] handle on/off pair (1294-g); three-argument arity (1294-h); synchronous post-fold dispatch with the per-runtime §4.1 re-entry cap of 8 (1294-c) terminating as a REJECTED INTENT rather than a stack overflow; CXER4851 as the subscriber-rejection channel exactly as xap.md §8 declares it - a handler that RETURNS an [err] rejects the act and the err flows out of emit, while a handler that FAULTS does not (the handler is broken, the act is not); and run\'s handlers: option, declared in the run-option table since the surface existed and read by nothing (1294-d). Every case red-proved against the pre-fix binary with the pre-fix answer quoted IN the case. Two cases (004 non-match, 008 unquoted $x) are GREEN PRE-FIX and say so in as many words: they are negative controls, and a suite of only positive cases cannot distinguish a working matcher from one that fires on everything. Hermetic: every runtime is UNBOUND (no journal: option) - no store, no socket, no capability grant - so these cases pin the flowing-[err] half of CXER4851 and the appended-rejection-event half rides the journal-bound cases in vcx/tests/xap_umbrella_test.v. NOT covered here and named rather than left silent: run\'s CLOSED option set (1294-d\'s second half) and the batch lane\'s per-act prep recompute (1294-c\'s second half), both of which are the next RULED pieces of 1294-f\'s stated landing order.']

    [# spec-first frontier, ahead of the code (#1422; RULED: 1422-a) #]
    [module name=audit gate=enforced reason='cx-platform/audit — the audit sink (spec/03-approved/platform/audit.md §9; #1422, RULED: 1422-a/1422-b). ENFORCED as of the commit that landed stdlib/audit.cx + vcx/platform/stdlib_audit.v: the corpus was written BEFORE the module on purpose (the zip hostile-container and saml XSW precedent, RULED: S-2; the order 1085-a and #1413 restate) and that red list WAS the implementation worklist, so the row flips here together with audit.md status=new -> current and the cx-stdlib module count, the mailbox (#1413) and sasl/smtp/imap (#1085) precedent. The eight attack classes of §7 — identifier injection, detail bombs, erasure-vocabulary smuggling, decision and module forgery, the unbound fallback as a smuggling channel, query evasion, foreign rows on the reserved stream, paging under concurrent append — are graded here, and so is the RULED: 1422-b reservation (a hand-authored append to cx:audit refuses journals own CXER4623). Hermetic: every Ring 2 case rides a mem:// journal, which is capability-free, so the whole file runs under the EMPTY capability set with no grant= anywhere, no port and no clock (audit.md §6.1: this module never reads one). No case pins a chain hash — those bytes are journal.cxd journal-079s.']

    [# the x/ tier (stream 18, L144/G17 — EXPLICIT rows, never silent
       default coverage; experimental status is a stability posture, not a
       gate posture: every x-tier suite is enforced) #]
    [module name=run        gate=enforced reason='Runnable convention + combinators (x/run.md §6): invoke/batch/pipe/compose/fan-out + the post-#45 nested-pipe case.']
    [module name=llm        gate=enforced reason='pure shaping + extractors (x/llm.md); the effectful lane is the live mock-server round-trip vcx/tests/llm_real_test.v.']
    [module name=tools      gate=enforced reason='the agent-tool projection (x/tools.md; stream 18): the refund-order golden descriptor (M5), fail-loud missing-summary, the effects-presence discriminator (zero-item included), rest-param additionalProperties, carrier conventions, requires/idempotent carriage, malformed-source propagation. Goldens binary-derived.']
    [module name=mcp        gate=enforced reason='client shapes + validate-args + the 2025-06-18 protocol pin mcp-007 (x/mcp.md §1 — one target, stream 18 L138); live round-trip vcx/tests/mcp_real_test.v.']
    [module name=mcp-server gate=enforced reason='server shapes + THE tools/list refund-order golden (007) + fail-loud propagation (008) + the propose-only reply golden (009) + the never-executes out-effects discriminator (010) (x/mcp-server.md; stream 18 L138/L141/L142/L113/L139/L140); live server + capability denial vcx/tests/mcp_server_real_test.v.']
    [module name=a2a        gate=enforced reason='client shapes + skills derived from the SAME projection (a2a-008 golden; a2a-009 fail-loud) — the hardcoded-empty skills list is dead (x/a2a.md §2; stream 18 L141/#715); live round-trip vcx/tests/a2a_real_test.v.']
    [module name=a2a-xap    gate=enforced reason='tasks→journal + messages→bus + auth→did/vc, hermetic (mem:// journal, fresh keypair); the durable pending-approval case a2a-xap-008 (input-required carries the proposal Tier-1 address through replay) + the approval-credential case 009 (x/a2a-xap.md §2/§3; stream 18 L140).']
    [module name=adjudicate gate=enforced reason='pure verdict/record/prompt-structure surface (x/adjudicate.md); the effectful lane is the live mock /api/chat round-trip vcx/tests/adjudicate_real_test.v.']
    [module name=ux         gate=enforced reason='the web UX projection emitter core (#787 W1, design/787/787-phase0-spec.md — owner-RULED 2026-08-17). The three W1 lanes from that spec §7: rendered-fragment goldens (fragment identity is EXACTLY (route, feature instance, element path) — theme/locale/actor/data are content, never identity; the DOM id is cx- plus hash16 of the address canonical bytes with the readable form in data-cx-frag; keyed rows are individually addressable and UNKEYED rows get no address rather than a positional one), the subset-list fixture (the pinned 11 htmx attributes, hx-on excluded permanently — enforced twice: the name gate at authorship and a re-scan of the serialized bytes, so any off-list attribute in emitter output is red), and escaping/CSP (structural escaping via a single [$html:serialize] over a composed CXDM tree — no interpolation surface exists; strict CSP with default-src none and each vendored script pinned by the SRI of the bytes actually served; an external src-bearing script is sanctioned, an inline one refuses). Plus the refusal surface (unknown element, mixed content, bad heading level, bad tone, verbless action, featureless region, id collision, unsafe theme token, and route/resource drift in BOTH directions), the token-theme stylesheet, and the asset manifest deny-by-default lane. Goldens binary-derived. Runnable surface: design/787/w1/.']]

