     CXPath / XPath 3.1 alignment corpus. Single-file suite — no module rows,
     the suite default governs the whole file (the `code` shape). Consumer:
     scripts/check_xpath_parity_fixtures.cx (gate 28.5a, in TEST_TARGETS), which
     resolves per-case gate= > this default > the [gate-policy] default and
     EXITS 2 if this row is missing — a lane whose tier is invisible is the
     class of defect #945 filed. The Saxon-HE cross-check (gate 28.5b) is a
     MANUAL row and is not governed here; see conformance/GATE_REGISTER.md. #]
